# AGP policy-enforcement surfaces, hash-pinned by @intentsolutions/audit-harness.
#
# AGP has none of the harness's default-pinned files (.feature, dependency-cruiser,
# stryker, .c8rc) — its policy lives in these files instead. Any byte change to one
# of them requires a deliberate re-pin (`scripts/audit-harness init`); `verify` in
# pre-commit + CI blocks an un-re-pinned edit, so a gate or claim rule cannot be
# silently weakened in a PR.

# The v0 marketing-claim registry (Epic 11: "hash-pinned in the harness manifest").
MARKETING_CLAIMS.md

# Gate logic + thresholds — lowering a floor or removing a gate is an escape attempt.
scripts/coverage-gate.sh
scripts/claim-scan.sh
scripts/doc-drift.sh
scripts/pre-commit-gates.sh

# Test policy + requirements traceability (engineer-owned; MUST tiers must not drop).
tests/TESTING.md
tests/RTM.md

# Lint / coverage config.
.markdownlint.json
bunfig.toml
biome.json

# Mutation testing config (informational posture; thresholds.break=null until baseline set).
# Pinned so any silent loosening of scope or threshold is caught by verify.
stryker.config.json

# BDD/acceptance layer spec (J1 operator journey, INV-1 through INV-6).
# Human-owned: changes require deliberate re-pin via `scripts/audit-harness init`.
# The diff-grep gate excludes tests/features/** (INITIAL CREATION); hash-verify
# is the load-bearing integrity check going forward.
tests/features/J1-governed-session.feature

# Architecture rules (layering invariants enforced by `audit-harness arch`).
.dependency-cruiser.cjs

# Release-readiness gate (Epic 15). Pinned so a silent loosening is caught by verify.
scripts/release-validate.sh
